{"kind":"request","text":"Builder: add a safe, reversible binary and service upgrade path without touching Tailapp sources or projection data.","body":{"conditions":"Depends on first-time setup. At a reviewed exact head, the installer/upgrade surface stages a verified release in a versioned user-owned directory, retains a known-good prior binary, atomically switches a stable current target used by the service, restarts, and rolls back to the prior target if control-plane startup fails. It must distinguish a running healthy control plane from ingestion_ready: a runtime-profile mismatch is an expected, prominently reported app-upgrade requirement, not a failed binary upgrade or an excuse to auto-reactivate apps. By default an upgrade must not install new bundles, rewrite any app source, activate any app, reset a projection, or modify telemetry configuration. Provide a machine-readable upgrade/status result and clear manual next commands; test failed-start rollback and the upgrade-pending case.","to":"00721374a520eabbbd4ded64dd018110f47545ff20112bee83c75f478e15f818"}}